WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.700
Behind everything that has ever happened, is happening, or ever will happen, there is a gradient.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.780
We are slaves to the gradient.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.880
This episode was made possible by generous supporters on Patreon.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.840
Ok, crazies.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.320
Before we get too nihilistic here, let's ask a proper question:

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.620
Um, what’s a gradient?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.080
Yes! This is going to be fun.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.920
Let’s start with the definition.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.980
The gradient represents the greatest increase in a number across space.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.940
Hmm, greatest increase, what can we do with this.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.960
Say you’re standing on a hill.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.400
You could move north, south, east, west, or some combination those.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.300
At each location, you have an elevation measured vertically from the bottom of the hill.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.020
So, now we've got a bunch of numbers assigned to different points in space.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.560
Wait a minute!

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.140
That's what we call a field.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.740
A number or set of numbers assigned to each point in space.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:01.540
In this case, the number is elevation so we'll call this an elevation field.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.440
Any direction you move on the hill will change that elevation.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.679
The direction of the gradient is the direction you can walk

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.520
that will give you the quickest change in elevation.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.880
But this gradient also depends on location, so it's also a field.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.800
Just like the elevation is a number assigned to each point in space,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.380
the gradient is an arrow assigned to each point in space.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.079
The direction of each of those arrows is the direction of greatest increase in elevation

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.680
and their size tells us how quickly that increase is happening.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.180
At this point though, some of you might be wondering:

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.740
But, like why does any of this matter?

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.760
Because it tells us what's going to happen.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.720
Elevation isn't the only number we assign to points in space.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.700
Say you've got a tank full of water.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.520
Let's imagine the water is made of very tiny water cubes.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.620
Each of those cubes has a pressure exerted on it from the surrounding cubes.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.020
We'll measure that pressure as a number
and assign it to the cube

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.020
and we'll do the same for all the other
cubes in the tank.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.940
This is something we might call a pressure field.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:06.360
Just like we did with elevation, we have a pressure assigned to points in space.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.320
It's not perfectly uniform throughout the tank though.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.860
It's higher at the bottom than it is at the top.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.170
That's what we call a pressure gradient

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.790
and it points in the direction of greatest increase.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.100
In this case, straight downward.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.180
That gradient is important because pressure can control what happens.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.620
The gradient of a pressure is a force!

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.860
Actually, when you work out the units, you
get a force density not a force.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.080
Close enough!

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.400
Also, force isn't the positive gradient.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.780
It's the negative gradient.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.340
Remind me again why you had to come back from vacation.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.600
I missed you.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.380
Ok, ok, back to the tank!

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.460
Say we put something else into the tank, like a bowling ball.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.380
It's going to experience the pressures from the surrounding water cubes,

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.020
but those pressures are larger on the bottom
than on the top.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.140
This results in an upward force

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.380
per unit volume.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.500
Much better.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.340
That bowling ball is displacing a particular volume of water.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.880
The pressure gradient across that volume gives us a force:

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.260
Something we call a buoyant force.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:08.560
If that buoyant force is strong enough to
overpower gravity,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.240
the bowling ball will float.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.600
Yes, some bowling balls float.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.500
The heavier ones sink, but the lighter ones can float

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.700
if they're under 12 pounds or so.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.800
The reason that happens is because of a pressure gradient.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.280
For that matter, it's why a lot of things happen.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.080
It's what allows you to breathe.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.900
It's what creates wind.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.620
And it’s why a portal between Denver and New York would be a very bad idea.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.260
But that bowling ball example had another force in it:

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.500
Gravity, which is also the result of a gradient.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.960
An energy gradient.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.120
Technically speaking, a pressure is an energy density,

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.460
so a pressure gradient is an energy gradient.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.060
I'm not sure that insight is helpful here, but thanks?

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.160
So energy gradients.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.850
At every possible location inside this tank,

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.980
the bowling ball has an energy given to it by the Earth.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.760
Those energies increase as you move up in the tank,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.460
so the energy gradient is straight upward.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.200
This gradient causes a force and, as Nerd Clone mentioned,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.400
that force will be the negative or opposite of the gradient.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.320
It'll point downward which is exactly what you’d expect for gravity.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.250
Mathematically, we'd write the gradient like this:

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.160
The change in energy over the distance in the upward direction.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.040
To get the force of gravity, we just take the negative or opposite of that.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.020
That means gravity points in the direction of greatest decrease in energy, which is downward.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.940
This is a really simple example though.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.100
The energy only changes in one direction.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.200
In some other example, it might change in two directions or even three.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.020
We do live in a three dimensional space, after all.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:44.540
If we add a term for each of the other directions, we get this.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.540
Of course, that looks kind of nasty,

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.920
so we relabel it with a single symbol:

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.280
The Nabla.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:53.160
It's an old Greek word for harp apparently.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.160
I guess it kinda looks like a harp,

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.840
but it's really just an upside down delta for change.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.720
A change in some number across space.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.520
Lots of measurements can be different in different places

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.600
and those differences are what cause things to happen.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.560
Weather patterns on the Earth are caused by pressure and temperature gradients.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.340
Buoyancy is caused a pressure gradient.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:17.800
Newtonian Gravity is caused an energy gradient.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.260
Yeah yeah, I know, gravity is really the curvature of spacetime, but there's still a gradient.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.400
It's just a little beyond this video.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.160
Concentration gradients are a way cells exchange molecules with their surroundings.

00:05:29.169 --> 00:05:31.580
We call it passive transport.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.560
Fluid motion? Gradient.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.700
Brain function? Gradient.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.560
Electromagnetic interactions? Gradient!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.420
The eventual heat death of the universe is literally the end of all gradients.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.900
If there's no more gradients, that's it.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.980
That's the end.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.880
Nothing will ever happen again ever.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.100
Probably.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:56.700
Behind everything that has ever happened, is happening, or ever will happen, there is a gradient.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.720
We are slaves to the gradient.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.760
All hail the gradient!

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.320
So how do you feel about this?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.260
Are you ok being a slave to the gradient?

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.110
Or do you think we have the ability to rise above it?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.960
Please share your thoughts in the comments.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.820
Thanks for liking and sharing this video.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.820
A special thanks goes out to Patreon patrons like Ken Davis

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.460
who help keep this show going with their generous support.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:17.780
Don't forget to subscribe if you'd like to keep up with us.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.300
And until next time, remember, it's ok to be a little crazy.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.080
To everyone who commented about perpetual motion machines:

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.800
No, those don't suddenly become possible.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:31.980
Even though more dark energy is being created over time,

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:35.040
it remains perfectly uniform throughout space,

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.460
which means there's no gradient,

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:37.980
which means we can't use it.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.560
Anyway, thanks for watching.

